{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"0c0b6f55-ac2a-41e1-9b9e-89ab7f7f6d1d","title":"Venn diagram for the union of two events"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"0c0b6f55-ac2a-41e1-9b9e-89ab7f7f6d1d","step":{"id":"s1","script":"The rectangle contains all possible outcomes. Circles A and B represent two events, and their overlap contains outcomes belonging to both.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Union of two events"},{"op":"figure","id":"venn","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-4.5,4.5],"y":[-2.8,2.8],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"polyline","id":"sample","points":[[-4,-2.3],[4,-2.3],[4,2.3],[-4,2.3]],"closed":true},{"kind":"circle","id":"event_a","center":[-1,0],"r":1.7},{"kind":"circle","id":"event_b","center":[1,0],"r":1.7},{"kind":"text","at":[-1.7,0.7],"text":"A"},{"kind":"text","at":[1.7,0.7],"text":"B"},{"kind":"text","at":[-3.5,1.9],"text":"S"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"0c0b6f55-ac2a-41e1-9b9e-89ab7f7f6d1d","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The union means A or B, including both. Shade all of each circle; the overlap is included, not excluded.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"union_fill","on":"venn","marks":[{"kind":"shade","inside":"event_a"},{"kind":"shade","inside":"event_b"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"union_rule","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"A\\cup B=\\{\\text{outcomes in A or B or both}\\}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"0c0b6f55-ac2a-41e1-9b9e-89ab7f7f6d1d","step":{"id":"s3","script":"These three outcomes all belong to the union: A only, both events, and B only. The outcome outside both circles does not.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"examples","on":"venn","marks":[{"kind":"point","at":[-2,0],"label":"1"},{"kind":"point","at":[0,0],"label":"2"},{"kind":"point","at":[2,0],"label":"3"},{"kind":"point","at":[3.2,-1.7],"label":"4"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"membership","anchor":{"el":"union_rule","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"1,2,3\\in A\\cup B,\\qquad 4\\notin A\\cup B"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Does outcome 2, in the overlap, belong to the union?","expected_gist":"Yes; the union includes outcomes in both events."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"0c0b6f55-ac2a-41e1-9b9e-89ab7f7f6d1d","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Adding event probabilities counts the overlap twice. Subtract it once so every outcome in the union is counted exactly once.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"overlap_note","on":"venn","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":[0,-1.9],"to":[0,-0.5],"arrow":true},{"kind":"text","at":[0,-2.1],"text":"count once","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"probability","anchor":{"el":"membership","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"P(A\\cup B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B)"}],"checkpoint":null}}
